{"name":"Beggar","hex":"#5a4d39","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beggar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who begs.","A person suffering from extreme poverty."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a beggar of someone; impoverish.","To exhaust the resources of; to outdo or go beyond."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beggar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Begging","blocks":[{"text":"Begging is the practice of imploring others to grant a favor, often a gift of money, with little or no expectation of reciprocation. A person doing such is called a beggar or panhandler. Beggars may operate in public places such as transport routes, urban parks, and markets. Besides money, they may also ask for food, drink, cigarettes or other small items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Beggars_in_the_street_2.JPG/330px-Beggars_in_the_street_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Begging","wikidata":"Q17572748"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg/500px-A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg/1280px-A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg/500px-A_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Begging directed at passing traffic, Denver, Colorado, 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_beggar_in_Denver%2C_USA_in_2018.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Woman_begging.jpg/500px-Woman_begging.jp